<title>UK: Railtrack says raised traffic capacity.</title>
<headline>Railtrack says raised traffic capacity.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British railway infrastructure operator Railtrack Plc said on Thursday it had increased the traffic-handling capacity of the rail network and reduced train delays in the six months to March 1997.</p>
<p>In its latest review, Railtrack said more of the network was able to carry international freight loads and routes from London to Scotland, Wales, the Midlands and Plymouth had been prepared for Channel Tunnel trains.</p>
</text>
